# Data Fetching — Custom Hooks Per Resource

Each API resource has its own custom hook(s) in `src/hooks/`. Hooks use a hand-rolled `useState` + `useEffect` + axios pattern (no TanStack Query). Page components call hooks; they **never** call `api` directly.

```js
// ✅ Existing hooks — use these, don't bypass them
useLetters(sortBy, sortOrder, statusFilter, searchQuery)  // GET /{firmId}/letters/
useDeleteLetter()                                         // DELETE /{firmId}/letters/:id
useExportLetter()                                         // POST /{firmId}/letters/:id/export
useDocuments(sortBy, sortOrder)                           // GET /{firmId}/documents/
useDocumentUpload()                                       // POST /{firmId}/documents/
useDocumentDelete()                                       // DELETE /{firmId}/documents/:id
useDocumentDownload()                                     // GET /{firmId}/documents/:id/download
useTemplates()                                            // GET /{firmId}/templates/
useLetterGeneration()                                     // POST /generate/letter
useLetterFinalize()                                       // POST /{firmId}/letters/:id/finalize
```

### Hook Shape Convention

All data-fetching hooks return `{ data, loading, error, refetch }` or a similar named shape. Mutation hooks return `{ mutate, loading, error }`. Keep naming consistent.

```js
// ✅ GOOD
const { letters, loading, error, refetch } = useLetters();
const { deleteLetter, deleting, error } = useDeleteLetter();

// ❌ BAD — calling the axios client directly from a component
const res = await api.get(`/${firmId}/letters/`);
```

### firmId Always Comes from useAuth

Every hook reads `user.firmId` from `useAuth()`. Never pass `firmId` as a prop or read it from `localStorage` directly in a component.

```js
// ✅ GOOD — hook handles auth context internally
export function useDocuments() {
  const { user } = useAuth();
  // ...uses user.firmId for the API path
}

// ❌ BAD — component reaching into auth state for API calls
const firmId = localStorage.getItem('firmId');
const res = await api.get(`/${firmId}/documents/`);
```

